The quantum eraser is a name given by the media to a series of
experiments done my Leonard Mandel at Rochester. Is is an
updated EPR type of experiment now possible thanks to lasers,
downconverters and other new technology. 

The best source I know is an article in the July 1992 Scientific
American. It has pictures and some explanation. You have one
laser split into four beams. Two are brought together on one
screen, and the other two on a distant screen. If one of the
four paths are blocked, you would expect the interference
pattern to go away on that one screen. The good part is that the
interference goes away on both screens. That means the photons
affect each other even though there is no physical connection.
The result is predicted my QM, but is still so weird that many
people are thrown into cognitive dissonance. It does not fit
with ones feeling of reality, either classical or the older QM
so useful in the past.
                                 
